  VALUES ('CORE', 12, 'Patient contact consent per channel in the QR consent (email, phone/SMS, WhatsApp)', 'We can''t lawfully send patient reminders without a recorded basis per channel. Today the QR consent has no contact-channel choice.', '* Add 3 separate, unticked checkboxes to the patient QR consent:
  * reminders by email;
  * by phone (SMS);
  * by WhatsApp (separate, as Meta requires explicit opt-in).
* Store them in the `consent` table: channel, given_at, the consent document version, and the source (QR/staff).
* Show the state on the patient record (read-only chips).
* A staff edit requires a reason and is audited.
* The sender checks consent before every patient delivery. Without consent there is no send, and the delivery is logged as `skipped_no_consent`.
* Full consent management (view, withdraw, history) is the separate Consents & Privacy epic.
* /legal review of the wording in PL and MX.',
    '* The checkboxes are in the PL/MX/EN QR form and saved to `consent`.
* A reminder to a patient without email consent is skipped and logged (test).
* The legal wording is signed off.', 'backlog', 2, ARRAY['Notifications', 'Feature']::text[],
    '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'linear_import', 'CORE-12', 'linear',
    '2026-09-27T01:07:13.214Z'::timestamptz, '2026-09-27T01:07:13.214Z'::timestamptz, '2026-09-27T01:07:13.214Z'::timestamptz, NULL)
