     source, linear_identifier, created_by, created_at, updated_at, status_changed_at, completed_at)
  VALUES ('CORE', 35, 'Flaky API tests: 3–4 intermittent failures under the full parallel run', 'Seen 2026-09-25 while running the API suite many times (fresh Postgres 15, `pnpm -r test` / pre-push hook) for the dependency upgrades ([NEO-67](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-67/dependency-major-upgrades-24-packages-7-groups)). Every one of these tests failed once in a full parallel run, then passed on its own and on retry. None relate to the upgrades:

* `routes/territory.spec.ts` › "403s a DELETE from a non-admin role"
* `routes/patient.spec.ts` › patient self-fill (QR) end to end over HTTP, "used link then answers 410"
* `auth.spec.ts` › "POST /api/v1/auth/login eventually 429s after repeated attempts from the same client". Likely a shared rate-limit bucket between parallel test files.
* `routes/practitionerOrganization.spec.ts` › "returns organizations\[\] and my_primary_organization_id…" (15 s timeout, once)

Impact: the pre-push hook and CI randomly block pushes and merges; people get used to "just retry".
Next step: find the shared state (rate-limiter memory store, shared test tenant rows, pool/connection timing) and isolate it. No retries and no `.skip`.', NULL,
    NULL, 'backlog', 3, '{}'::text[],
