  VALUES ('CORE', 36, 'Backup check: 7 nights green + decide on locking 30-day retention', 'One week after [NEO-62](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-62/nightly-encrypted-backup-of-supabase-db-storage-to-google-cloud) went live (2026-09-25).

## Check

- [ ] [https://github.com/lukasz512/NeoSleep/actions/workflows/nightly-backup.yml](<https://github.com/lukasz512/NeoSleep/actions/workflows/nightly-backup.yml>) — every nightly run since 2026-09-26 is green (no missed nights).
- [ ] [https://console.cloud.google.com/storage/browser/neosleep-backups-db](<https://console.cloud.google.com/storage/browser/neosleep-backups-db>) — one folder per day, each with `neosleep-db-*.dump.age` + `neosleep-storage-*.tar.gz.age`, sizes plausible (DB \~2–3 MB and growing, not shrinking to \~0).
- [ ] Try to delete one object in the console → must be refused (retention policy works).

## Decide (Łukasz)

- [ ] Lock the retention policy? Irreversible: nobody (incl. us) can shorten it or delete the bucket while it holds objects younger than 30 days. Protects backups even if the Google account is compromised. Command: `gcloud storage buckets update gs://neosleep-backups-db --lock-retention-period` (Cloud Shell, project neosleep-backups).

Runbook: docs/RUNBOOK_BACKUP_RESTORE.md', NULL,
