  VALUES ('CORE', 40, 'Doctor role: API returns only the doctor''s own patients', 'A user with role `doctor` must only ever see their own patients: the patients whose `practitioner_id` is the doctor''s own practitioner record. Decided by Łukasz on 2026-09-25.

## Today

* `GET /api/v1/patient` (`GetPatientListQuery`, apps/api/src/queries/patient.ts) filters only by an optional `practitioner_id` query param plus the RBAC territory `scopePaths`. There is no doctor-specific rule, so a doctor sees every patient in their territory.
* The route has only `requireAuth`. There are no doctor checks in the middleware or routes.
* A doctor account is linked to its practitioner through a shared identity: `users.identity_id` = `practitioner.identity_id` (ADR-014, provisioned by `POST /practitioner/:id/activate`).
* The [NEO-57](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-57/pwa-lists-shared-clinical-card-table-mobile-card-style) PWA already treats the doctor''s patient list as "my patients": the "Last updated" column replaces "Doctor".

## Scope

* **Resolve the practitioner server-side** from `ctx.user`''s identity and **force** `practitioner_id = <own>` on the patient list. Ignore or reject a client-supplied `practitioner_id` for doctors.
* **Detail endpoints:** `GET/PATCH /patient/:id` and patient sub-resources (notes, documents, studies, endo intake, STOP-BANG, history) return 404 for a patient that isn''t theirs.
  * Use 404, not 403, so the endpoint doesn''t reveal that the patient exists.
* **Related lists:** decide whether sleep studies and treatment plans get the same sco…', NULL,
    NULL, 'backlog', 2, ARRAY['blocked']::text[],
