  VALUES ('CORE', 41, 'Territory migration: retire region in favor of territory_id across identities + encounter (ADR needed)', 'Follow-up to [NEO-6](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-6/widok-hco). `region`/`territory_id` is a shared pair that exists in **three separate places** in the schema — not just `organization` (already handled in [NEO-6](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-6/widok-hco)):

1. `identities` — shared base table, used by `users` (internal reps/managers), `practitioner`, `patient`, `lead`. Touches `apps/api/src/{routes,queries,db}/{users,practitioner,patient,leads}.ts`.
2. `organization` — **done** in [NEO-6](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-6/widok-hco) (migration 026, form field removed).
3. `encounter` — visit records also carry their own `region`/`territory_id` pair (`apps/api/src/db/encounter.ts`).

Roughly 19 backend files total reference `region` across routes/queries/db, plus every FE form/list that filters or sorts by it. This is a real architecture decision, not a quick fix — needs an ADR before implementation, and should never go to the unattended nightly worker (touches `identities`/`patient`/`practitioner`, always-blocked per `linear-worker/SKILL.md` Step 4).

**Not in scope**: `booking.ts`''s `region` parameter — that''s an unrelated locale/country-code proxy via `localeForRegion`, not the territory concept. Don''t conflate the two again.

## Recommended approach: expand-contract, not big-bang

Proven pattern for retiring a live column safely, same technique [NEO-6](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-6/widok-hco)''s migration 026 already validated against rea…', NULL,
