  VALUES ('CORE', 43, 'PWA HCO location map: same broken Google Maps loader as the old website map', 'Found during [NEO-79](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-79/website-find-a-specialist-map-refactor-to-current-api-app-quality-and). The website''s old loader used `loading=async` and then called `new google.maps.Map` before the library existed ("[g.maps.Map](<http://g.maps.Map>) is not a constructor"), so the old website map never rendered. [NEO-79](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-79/website-find-a-specialist-map-refactor-to-current-api-app-quality-and) fixed this on the website (`apps/web/src/composables/useGoogleMaps.ts`, rewritten; branch `worktree-neo-79-specialist-map`).

The PWA''s `apps/pwa/src/composables/useGoogleMaps.ts` (used by `HCOLocationMap.vue`) appears to use the same loader, so it is probably broken in the same way. This is not verified.

## Scope

* Verify on pwa-dev: open an HCO with coordinates and check whether the map renders.
* If it is broken, port the [NEO-79](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-79/website-find-a-specialist-map-refactor-to-current-api-app-quality-and) loader fix. Ideally, share one loader between web and PWA.
* Replace the deprecated `google.maps.Marker` with `AdvancedMarkerElement`. This needs the Map ID (`VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID`) from [NEO-79](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-79/website-find-a-specialist-map-refactor-to-current-api-app-quality-and).', NULL,
