  VALUES ('CORE', 71, 'Nightly backup fails since 09-27: restore check needs btree_gist extension', 'The nightly backup has failed 3 nights in a row (09-27, 09-28, 09-29). The restore check fails with `uuid has no default operator class for access method "gist"` because migration 035 ([NEO-27](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-27/design-new-appointment-entity-for-patientdoctor-visits-rbac)) needs `btree_gist`, and the throwaway restore DB doesn''t create it. The check runs before upload, so no backup has reached gs://neosleep-backups-db since 09-26. Nobody saw the failure alerts.', '* Nightly backup workflow: run `CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS btree_gist` (plus any other extensions the tenant migrations use) in the restore DB before pg_restore.
