* Client-sent practitioner_id filter ignored for doctors
* Audit other entities for the same leak; the ones needing a product decision (practitioners, encounters, treatment-plan role line) moved to [CORE-109](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/CORE-109/doctor-access-to-non-patient-entities-practitioners-encounters)
* Integration tests on real DB: doctor A gets 404/403 on doctor B''s patient and every sub-resource',
    '- [ ] Doctor A cannot list, open or change doctor B''s patient or any of its sub-resources (tests)
- [ ] Admin/manager behavior unchanged (tests)
- [ ] Access matrix for every endpoint documented in the Artifact', 'done', 1, '{}'::text[],
    '[{"kind":"pr","url":"https://github.com/lukasz512/NeoSleep/pull/369","title":"CORE-104 Doctor sees only own patients — one access policy"},{"kind":"artifact","url":"https://claude.ai/artifact/1kDDV3sMY4Ld8GrLuQiMBf","title":"Artifact: CORE-104 Doctor Sees Only Own Patients"}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'linear_import', 'CORE-104', 'linear',
