  VALUES ('CORE', 122, 'Calendario: Mac-style day/week/month views with liquid glass and smooth transitions', 'The Calendario screen ([CORE-117](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/CORE-117/one-calendar-merge-planificador-and-citas-into-one-calendario-screen)) uses Vuetify VCalendar: day/week grid plus an agenda list, no month view, a flat toolbar, and the same layout on every screen size. Łukasz wants it to look and feel like macOS / iOS Calendar on desktop, tablet and phone. He approved the prototype: [https://claude.ai/artifact/K51FhhBB6wVHv5bLHVQs4e](<https://claude.ai/artifact/K51FhhBB6wVHv5bLHVQs4e>)', '* Replace VCalendar with our own time grid (day/week) and month grid. Same /api/v1/calendar data and the same dialogs (EventForm, AppointmentDialog, AppointmentDetailDialog).
* Floating liquid-glass toolbar (--glass-\* tokens from [NEO-161](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-161/mobile-menu-liquid-glass-kropla-bottom-nav-account-menu)) with a Día · Semana · Mes segmented control and a spring thumb.
* Desktop: sidebar with a mini month and filters by kind. Tablet: the sidebar opens as a glass panel. Phone: two-row header, a week that scrolls with snap, and a month with dots plus that day''s list.
* View Transitions: zoom in/out between month, week and day, slide for prev/next. Reduced motion turns this off.
* Now line, today marker, sticky glass day headers, a tap on a date opens that day.',
    '* Day, week and month render the real entries on pwa-dev, on desktop, tablet and phone widths
* Clicking an entry opens its existing dialog, and clicking an empty slot opens the add choice
* Unit tests cover layout (overlap lanes, week/month windows), and CalendarView.spec passes
* Before/after screenshots are in the Artifact', 'done', 2, '{}'::text[],
