  VALUES ('CORE', 129, 'Calendario phone: one header, + top-right, swipe between months', 'After [CORE-122](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/CORE-122/calendario-mac-style-dayweekmonth-views-with-liquid-glass-and-smooth) ([lukasz512/NeoSleep#403](https://linear.app/neosleep/review/core-122-calendario-mac-style-dayweekmonth-liquid-glass-transitions-92d6339dfcff)), the phone shows two headers: the app''s "Calendario" row and the calendar''s own glass bar. Both have a calendar icon, and the "+" isn''t in the top-right corner like in the other modules. Swiping left/right on the month does nothing because the browser takes the touch for scrolling.', '* Phone: hide the layout''s page-header row on /calendar (route meta flag) and keep the calendar''s glass bar as the only header.
* Glass bar icon in the module teal, like the page-header icon.
* Phone: "+" alone in the top-right corner (same look as other modules'' add); ‹ › arrows move to the second row next to Día/Semana/Mes.
* Swipe left/right on the month (and day) view goes to next/previous; touch-action pan-y so the browser leaves horizontal swipes to us.',
    '* On a phone, /calendar has one header; desktop is unchanged
* The "+" sits top-right and opens the add choice
* Swiping left on the month goes to the next month, swiping right to the previous one (test)
* Before/after phone screenshots in the Artifact', 'done', 2, '{}'::text[],
    '[{"kind":"pr","url":"https://github.com/lukasz512/NeoSleep/pull/410","title":"CORE-129 Calendario phone: one header, + top-right, swipe between months"},{"kind":"artifact","url":"https://claude.ai/artifact/KgQBpxiieoi7RQPADWC4b6","title":"Artifact: CORE-129 Calendario phone header"}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'linear_import', 'CORE-129', 'linear',
