     source, linear_identifier, created_by, created_at, updated_at, status_changed_at, completed_at)
  VALUES ('CORE', 148, 'PWA deploy ran ahead of the API → empty doctor lists on pwa-dev', '2026-10-05: after PR [lukasz512/NeoSleep#440](https://linear.app/neosleep/review/neo-tbd-doctors-estudios-and-tratamientos-lists-follow-the-care-f22434ccb772) ([NEO-245](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-245/doctors-estudios-and-tratamientos-lists-follow-the-care-protocol)) merged, the PWA deployed but "Deploy API (Cloud Run)" was cancelled by a GitHub runner outage ("job was not acquired by Runner"). pwa-dev ran the new list UI against the old API (image 6ab2e49): a doctor''s Estudios/Tratamientos showed only Paciente + "—", with empty columns and no chips. Reruns were cancelled the same way until the API went out with 69a93cb.', '(a) The doctor lists fall back to the old columns when the API response lacks the progress fields, with a test.
(b) deploy-pwa waits for, or is gated on, a successful deploy-api for the same SHA when the merge touches both (or the API contract).',
    '* A spec proves the fallback: a list response without progress fields renders the old columns, not empty cells.
* A workflow gate exists so the PWA for SHA X is not published while the API for X failed or was cancelled.', 'backlog', 0, '{}'::text[],
