Create PR: https://github.com/lukasz512/NeoSleep/compare/dev...worktree-core-159-next-visit-tile…', 'linear', 'import', '2026-10-05T23:51:16.791Z'::timestamptz FROM ins;
WITH ins AS (
  INSERT INTO platform.work_item
    (team_key, number, title, problem, change, done_when, status, priority, labels, links, branch,
     source, linear_identifier, created_by, created_at, updated_at, status_changed_at, completed_at)
  VALUES ('CORE', 160, 'History: patient''s confirm/decline and clinical entries show empty', 'When a patient confirms or declines a visit from the email link, the History tab shows nothing useful. The audit row is written, but `AUDIT_FIELD_ALLOWLIST` (queries/auditLog.ts) strips `patient_response`, so it reads as an empty, actor-less "appointment updated". Stopping emails (`appointment_emails`) behaves the same way. Clinical entries (Consent, care team, questionnaires and exams, checklist files, partner orders) and a change of the primary doctor (`practitioner_id`) also show empty for the same reason.', 'Stage 1 of the history-completeness audit:

* allowlist `patient_response` (Appointment) and `appointment_emails`/`practitioner_id` (Patient)
* allowlist the clinical entity types with non-clinical fields only
* show "Patient" as the actor when [metadata.actor](<http://metadata.actor>) = patient
* write readable headlines in EN/PL/MX

Stages 2 and 3 get their own tickets: the invite/signature trail, attachments, notes, the partner send, skipped reminders and retention.',
    '* After a patient confirms or declines, the patient''s History shows "Patient confirmed the visit" / "Patient can''t attend", with Patient as the actor
* Opt-out and a primary-doctor change are readable entries
* Clinical entries show what happened, never clinical content
* An API integration test on the real DB covers each case', 'done', 2, '{}'::text[],
    '[{"kind":"pr","url":"https://github.com/lukasz512/NeoSleep/pull/469","title":"Worktree core 160 history patient response"},{"kind":"spec","url":"https://claude.ai/artifact/B84BHQqL6dEWgCMfVeuf66","title":"Artifact: CORE-160 History: patient answers"}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'linear_import', 'CORE-160', 'linear',
    '2026-10-05T23:45:45.605Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-06T00:12:10.777Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-06T00:12:10.777Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-06T00:12:10.777Z'::timestamptz)
  ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
  RETURNING id
)
