  VALUES ('NEO', 25, 'linear-worker: fail-fast environment pre-flight before per-ticket work', '[NEO-6](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-6/widok-hco) cycled through the nightly worker 6 times over 2026-09-09→09-16 without landing. Root cause of most of the wasted effort: environment-wide problems (DB isolation canary hanging with no timeout in pass 5; a GitHub App 403 on `git push` in pass 6) were only discovered at the very end of a run, after Enrich + Implement + Self-check had already burned 15-30 minutes.', 'Add a new **Step 2.5: Environment Pre-flight** to `.claude/skills/linear-worker/SKILL.md`, run once per invocation, before claiming any ticket:

1. `DATABASE_URL` presence check (moved from today''s Step 7.1, logic unchanged).
2. DB isolation canary under an explicit timeout (fixes pass 5''s 10+ minute hang) — three distinct outcomes: permission-denied (pass, proceed), succeeds (security misconfig, block), timeout (new outcome, block fast with a clear "network reachability" message instead of hanging).
3. New: non-destructive `git push --dry-run` capability check — catches the exact GitHub App 403 pass 6 hit, in seconds instead of after full implementation.

If pre-flight fails: do not claim the selected ticket (leave it in `Ready for Worker` so FIFO order survives for the next run), comment the failure on it anyway so it''s visible, end the run.

Also strengthens Step 4''s compliance-block comment to always include a ready-to-paste approval template when one unambiguous scoped fix exists — passes 1-3 burned 2 extra cycles because "sprobuj jeszcze raz" comments didn''t satisfy the actual override mechanism.

Step 7''s self-check keeps its own (now timeout-wrapped) copy of the isolation canary as defense-in-depth, unchanged in spirit. **Step 4''s compliance gate and Step 8''s no-retry-on-failure policy are explicitly NOT being loosened** — this is purely about failing fast on infra problems, not a safety relaxation.

Docs: append an "Update, 2026-09-16" entry to `docs/ADR-019-nightly…',
