  VALUES ('NEO', 37, 'Login page shows blank gradient during session check — add loading state', 'When the pwa app loads, `apps/pwa/src/router/index.ts`''s `beforeEach` guard `await`s `auth.fetchSession()` before resolving navigation to `/login` (and to `/forgot-password`, and any `requiresAuth` route). Vue Router doesn''t render `<RouterView>`''s matched component until `next()` fires, so `AuthView.vue` (card, form, decorative orbs) never mounts during that wait. `App.vue` defaults to `PublicLayout` before the route resolves, so the animated background shows — but nothing inside it does. On Render''s free-tier cold start this blank gap can last several seconds.

Reported by Łukasz with a screenshot of the resulting blank-except-background login page.

## Proposed direction

Reuse the existing decorative orbs (`.auth-view__orb*` in `AuthView.vue`, `auth-view-orb-pulse` keyframe) as the loading indicator instead of a generic spinner — pulse them gently as soon as `PublicLayout` mounts, skipping the pop-in choreography, so something visibly alive appears immediately. Once `fetchSession()` resolves, hand off smoothly into `AuthView`''s existing entrance sequence.

## Scope

Applies to `/login`, `/forgot-password`, and any `requiresAuth` deep link — all three hit the same awaited `fetchSession()` guard.

Full enrichment (five-lens pass, acceptance criteria, open questions): `docs/stories/login-loading-state.md`

## Open questions (need a call before/while implementing)

* Where should the loading orbs live — moved into `PublicLayout`, or a new lightweight shared component rendere…', NULL,
