  VALUES ('NEO', 41, 'Real Husky pre-commit/pre-push hooks (lint+typecheck+test)', 'CLAUDE.md claims "Pre-commit: lint + typecheck + test" and "Do not bypass Husky hooks (--no-verify)" but `.husky/pre-commit` and `.husky/pre-push` don''t exist — `core.hooksPath` points at `.husky/_` (husky''s own bootstrap) with no actual hook files, so every local git hook silently no-ops. Found during a repo-robustness audit 2026-09-20.

Only real enforcement today: Claude Code''s own Stop hook (`quality-gate.sh`, session-scoped) and CI on PR (after push). A plain `git commit`/`git push` from a terminal is completely ungated.

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] `.husky/pre-commit` runs lint + typecheck scoped to staged/changed files, blocks commit on failure
- [ ] `.husky/pre-push` runs tests scoped to affected workspaces (mirror `quality-gate.sh`''s scoping), blocks push on failure
- [ ] Verified with a deliberate failing change from a plain terminal (not Claude Code)
- [ ] CLAUDE.md''s existing claims become true instead of aspirational

Full context: `docs/stories/data-flow-robustness-hardening.md` (Stream 1)', NULL,
