  VALUES ('NEO', 42, 'Fix create_tenant_schema() drift vs. later migrations (004-022)', '`apps/api`''s `create_tenant_schema()` Postgres function (migration 001, last redefined in 003) is stale relative to 13 later migrations (004, 005, 006, 008, 009, 010, 012, 015, 017, 018, 020, 021, 022) that alter existing tenant schemas via ad-hoc loops over `platform.tenants` without ever updating the function body. `apps/api/scripts/sync-test-schema.ts`''s own doc comment confirms this and works around it by cloning the live `neosleep` schema instead of calling the function.

Dormant today (single tenant "neosleep", always provisioned by replaying every migration in order) but a landmine for the planned white-label multi-tenant provisioning flow. `arch/SKILL.md`''s documented future `POST /platform/tenants` already correctly plans to "run all tenant migrations" rather than call this function — but the function''s name and continued existence invite a future implementer to call it directly without knowing this history, silently producing an incomplete tenant schema (missing e.g. `identities.region`, `lead.institution`).

Found during a repo-robustness audit 2026-09-20. **Needs** `/arch assess` **before implementation** — this is an architecture decision (patch the function in place vs. deprecate it in favor of the "replay full migration history" approach), not a mechanical fix.

## Acceptance Criteria

