  VALUES ('NEO', 45, 'Investigate & fix apps/api slowness on Render (free plan)', 'Łukasz reports apps/api ("neosleep-bff" on Render) feels very slow, tested from Spain (not just MX). Current setup:

* `render.yaml`: `plan: free`, `region: frankfurt`
* Confirmed via the prod PWA bundle: `pwa.neosleepcare.com` actually calls `https://neosleep-bff.onrender.com` — the **same single Render service that tracks the** `dev` **branch**. There is no separate prod API deployment today, despite a `RENDER_API_URL_PROD` secret existing in CI.

## Hypothesis

Render''s free plan has both (a) spin-down after \~15 min idle (cold start, \~30-60s wake) and (b) throttled/shared CPU that could cause consistent slowness under any real load, not just on first request. Manual `/health` timing just now showed \~0.2-0.5s (no dramatic cold-start observed at that moment) — inconclusive; need a real idle-gap test and a heavier (DB/bcrypt-backed) endpoint test to isolate cause before spending on a migration.

## Scope (incremental, cheapest-first)

1. Diagnose: confirm/rule out cold-start vs. sustained-throttle vs. network-distance as the dominant cause.
2. Cheap stopgap ($0): scheduled keep-alive ping (GitHub Actions cron) to `/health` to prevent Render free-tier spin-down, if cold-start turns out to be a real factor.
3. If stopgap doesn''t fix it (throttle/compute-bound): evaluate migrating apps/api off Render to a $5/month Docker-based host ([Railway.io](<http://Railway.io>) Hobby evaluated — see docs/stories/api-hosting-migration-render-to-railway.md for full write-up, open question…', NULL,
