  VALUES ('NEO', 46, 'Doctor role: restrict patient access to own patients only (API-level)', '**Security fix — data access control.** A `doctor`-role user can currently list/fetch (and edit) *any* patient within their territory scope via `GET /patient`, `GET /patient/:id`, and the corresponding write routes — there is no server-side check tying results to the caller''s own identity. ADR-014 explicitly named "doctor sees only their own facility/patients" as deferred backend work; this ticket closes it.

Full refined story: `docs/stories/doctor-role-own-patients-row-scoping.md`

**Scope (confirmed 2026-09-21):**

* Read AND write together: `GET /patient`, `GET /patient/:id`, and `PUT`/`PATCH /patient/:id` all get the same ownership check (doctor → own `practitioner_id`-linked patients only).
* 403 Forbidden on cross-doctor access (consistent with the existing territory-scoping precedent from PR [lukasz512/NeoSleep#102](https://linear.app/neosleep/review/securitytoken-rotation-and-region-scoping-f717d14e8249)), not 404.
* Layered on top of existing territory scoping, not replacing it — other roles (rep/kam/msl/manager/admin) unaffected.
* Fail closed: a doctor with no linked `practitioner` row gets an empty result set, not unrestricted access.
* Real-Postgres integration tests required (no mock-only API tests, per CLAUDE.md).

Reference NEO-<n> in the PR body — no `Fixes`/`Closes`/`Resolves` (standing team convention, see CLAUDE.md Linear traceability section).', NULL,
