  VALUES ('NEO', 47, 'PATCH /patient/:id missing territory scoping check (all roles)', '**Found while implementing** [NEO-46](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-46/doctor-role-restrict-patient-access-to-own-patients-only-api-level) (doctor-own-patient scoping). `UpdatePatientCommand` (`apps/api/src/commands/patient.ts`) fetches the existing patient via `getPatientById` but never calls `assertTerritoryAccessByTerritoryId` — unlike `GetPatientByIdQuery`, which does. Any authenticated role (rep/kam/msl/manager, not just doctor) can currently edit a patient outside their assigned territory via `PATCH /patient/:id`, even though reading that same patient by ID is already correctly blocked.

Fix: add the same `assertTerritoryAccessByTerritoryId(ctx, before.territory_id)` check to `UpdatePatientCommand`, right after the existing `before = await getPatientById(...)` fetch — mirrors the read-path pattern already in `queries/patient.ts`.

Deliberately scoped separately from [NEO-46](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-46/doctor-role-restrict-patient-access-to-own-patients-only-api-level) (different vulnerability class — territory/geography, not doctor-identity ownership — and affects all roles, not just doctor). Real-Postgres integration test required per CLAUDE.md.', NULL,
