  VALUES ('NEO', 61, 'PWA spacing scale + shell rhythm (gutters, record header, tabs, bottom bar)', 'The patient record card (and the app shell as a whole) feels cramped. The root cause is that there is no spacing scale: about 351 spacing values are set by hand, many of them off-grid (6, 10, 14, 21px).

Proposal artifact: [https://claude.ai/artifact/PBs9hFYEXFm5kBHVaL5cR4](<https://claude.ai/artifact/PBs9hFYEXFm5kBHVaL5cR4>)

## Scope

* One 4-px spacing scale (`--space-*`) and a responsive `--page-gutter` (20px phone / 24px tablet / 32px desktop), shared by the PWA and @neo/ui
* Record header ([NEO-56](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-56/pwa-record-header-with-breadcrumb-salesforceveeva-pattern-patient-date)) rhythm: tile ↔ name, header → tabs, action buttons at 44px with an 8px gap
* Detail tabs: desktop gets a width that looks intentional (no 600px cap with equal-width, truncated slots); mobile pattern to be chosen from the proposal options
* History timeline rhythm (entries, day groups)
* Mobile bottom bar: grid spacing; on tablet, max-width for the icon row so items don''t spread across the whole width
* A guard spec against new off-scale spacing

## Decided

* Builds on [NEO-56](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-56/pwa-record-header-with-breadcrumb-salesforceveeva-pattern-patient-date) (PR [lukasz512/NeoSleep#184](https://linear.app/neosleep/review/neo-56-record-header-with-breadcrumb-salesforceveeva-pattern-df4ffe99dfdc), still open; this branch is stacked on it)
* Mobile tab pattern: pending Łukasz''s pick from the options in the artifact

Plain reference, no…', NULL,
