  VALUES ('NEO', 62, 'Nightly encrypted backup of Supabase DB + Storage to Google Cloud Storage', 'Supabase is on the **Free plan**, which gives no restorable backups. The DB holds medical data (patients, sleep studies, treatment plans) and Supabase Storage holds sleep-study attachments. Today nothing protects against data loss (bad migration, accidental delete, provider incident, account compromise).

## Decision (Łukasz, 2026-09-25)

* Keep Supabase (Free) for now; nightly backup comes first, API move to Google Cloud Run (near the DB) is a separate follow-up (see [NEO-45](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-45/investigate-and-fix-appsapi-slowness-on-render-free-plan)).
* Nightly job via **GitHub Actions scheduled workflow** (not a Claude routine — mechanical task, no LLM value, keeps medical data off extra systems).
* Retention: **30 days**.

## Scope

1. Nightly `pg_dump` (custom format) of the whole Supabase DB (all tenant schemas + `platform` + `public`).
2. Nightly copy of Supabase Storage buckets (sleep-study attachments etc.).
3. Encrypt client-side before upload (dump never leaves the runner unencrypted).
4. Upload to a Google Cloud Storage bucket (neosleep GCP project) with retention lock / object versioning, 30-day lifecycle.
5. Automated restore check on **every nightly run** (fresh dump restored into a throwaway Postgres service container, table count per app schema must match; run fails before upload otherwise). Decryption is tested by a manual quarterly drill with the offline key — an automated weekly decrypt-from-GCS test would require putting the privat…', NULL,
    NULL, 'needs_review', 1, '{}'::text[],
    '[{"kind":"pr","url":"https://github.com/lukasz512/NeoSleep/pull/193","title":"NEO-62: run backup Storage export on Node 22"},{"kind":"pr","url":"https://github.com/lukasz512/NeoSleep/pull/192","title":"NEO-62: Nightly encrypted backup of Supabase DB + Storage to GCS"}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'linear_import', 'NEO-62', 'linear',
    '2026-09-25T11:08:19.560Z'::timestamptz, '2026-09-25T11:08:19.560Z'::timestamptz, '2026-09-25T11:08:19.560Z'::timestamptz, NULL)
