  VALUES ('NEO', 77, 'OrthoApnea resources: videos and document links never load on deployed PWA', 'Reported by Łukasz 2026-09-25 on pwa-dev after the [NEO-45](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-45/investigate-and-fix-appsapi-slowness-on-render-free-plan) Cloud Run move ("nie mogę uruchomić ich filmów").

## Root cause (verified in code)

`services/partners/orthoapnea.ts:391,445` returns `mediaUrl` as a **relative** path (`/api/v1/partners/orthoapnea/resources/:id/media?...`). `ResourcesView.vue:105` puts it straight into `<video :src>` and `<a :href>`:

1. On deployed PWAs the relative URL resolves against the static GoDaddy host ([pwa-dev.neosleepcare.com](<http://pwa-dev.neosleepcare.com>)), not the API, so it 404s. Locally the Vite proxy hides this.
2. The `/media` route is `requireAuth` (bearer token). `<video>` and plain `<a>` requests cannot send an `Authorization` header, so even with the right host they get 401. Cookies were removed in ADR-020.

The resources list itself works (GET /resources returns 200 with a valid OrthoApnea login, checked in the Cloud Run logs).

## Direction (to decide in /enrich-user-story)

* Short-lived signed media URL: API issues a per-resource token (e.g. 5 min, bound to user + resource id), media route accepts `?t=`, and the frontend prefixes the API base URL. Works with `<video>` streaming and range requests.
* Alternative: fetch → blob → object URL. Simple, but loads the whole video into memory before play. Poor for large videos on phones.

## Acceptance

* A video plays inline on pwa-dev, and seeking works.
* A document link open…', NULL,
