  VALUES ('NEO', 80, 'pwa-dev login blank: two vue-router copies in the prod build after NEO-70', '**Regression on pwa-dev since PR** [lukasz512/NeoSleep#215](https://linear.app/neosleep/review/neo-70-major-upgrade-vue-router-5-pinia-4-vue-i18n-11-47bd70861cb2) **(**[NEO-70](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-70/major-upgrade-vue-router-5-pinia-4-vue-i18n-11)**):** the login page shows only the background. The form never renders, so nobody can sign in.

**Cause:** pnpm resolved `vue-router@5.3.1` twice, with different peer sets. `apps/pwa` and `packages/ui` each got their own copy, and the production build bundles both. `AuthView` (packages/ui) calls `useRoute()` against the other copy''s injection key, gets `undefined`, and crashes with `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading ''query'')`.

Dev mode (and so the e2e suite) prebundles a single copy, which is why tests passed.

**Fix:** add `resolve.dedupe` for vue, vue-router, pinia and vue-i18n in `apps/pwa/vite.config.ts`. Verified on a local production build: the login form renders again.

This was found while verifying [NEO-76](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-76/pwa-toasts-record-context-design-entity-icon-record-line-retry-action) on pwa-dev after its merge.

Also seen, not fixed here ([NEO-45](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-45/investigate-and-fix-appsapi-slowness-on-render-free-plan) area): the Cloud Run dev API answers `GET /health` without an `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header, so the browser blocks that one call. Login''s CORS preflight is fine.', NULL,
    NULL, 'done', 1, '{}'::text[],
    '[{"kind":"pr","url":"https://github.com/lukasz512/NeoSleep/pull/224","title":"NEO-80 pwa-dev login blank: dedupe vue-router in the prod build"},{"kind":"artifact","url":"https://claude.ai/artifact/4XZ4rAxPXo6Q9zuPTY6omE","title":"Artifact: NEO-80 pwa-dev Login Fix"}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'linear_import', 'NEO-80', 'linear',
