VS Code: vscode://anthropic.claude-code/open?session=b04ecf89-dc85-4025-9725-d8be9fccc55…', 'linear', 'import', '2026-09-26T16:45:40.929Z'::timestamptz FROM ins;
WITH ins AS (
  INSERT INTO platform.work_item
    (team_key, number, title, problem, change, done_when, status, priority, labels, links, branch,
     source, linear_identifier, created_by, created_at, updated_at, status_changed_at, completed_at)
  VALUES ('NEO', 101, 'Estudios: repeat patient questionnaires + doctor picks forms for the QR', '**Problem (Łukasz, 2026-09-26):** the same patient studies/questionnaires must be repeatable (e.g. follow-up after treatment). The doctor who generates the QR should choose which forms the patient gets.

**Today (origin/dev):**

* The API already accepts `items` on `POST …/questionnaire-requests` (CreateQuestionnaireRequestCommand) and records are append-only (one row per fill), so repeats are possible on the data side.
* The UI only offers "everything still missing". Once an item is done it is not offered again, and after "Todo recibido" the QR button hides ([NEO-93](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-93/estudios-qr-button-absorbs-the-pending-link-banner-status-button)).
* Patient-fillable items: informed consent, medical history, S-T-O-P.

**Change (to be scoped):** a form picker when generating the QR (and email link), which also allows already completed forms to be requested again; the Estudios checklist shows repeated fills as history.

**Depends on:** [NEO-93](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-93/estudios-qr-button-absorbs-the-pending-link-banner-status-button) (PR [lukasz512/NeoSleep#261](https://linear.app/neosleep/review/neo-93-estudios-qr-button-carries-the-link-status-one-live-link-per-4ded7c4e1bfb), QR status button, one live link per patient) — same UI.

Open questions are in the decision form (link in comments).', NULL,
    NULL, 'building', 0, '{}'::text[],
    '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'linear_import', 'NEO-101', 'linear',
    '2026-09-26T15:32:37.635Z'::timestamptz, '2026-09-26T15:32:37.635Z'::timestamptz, '2026-09-26T15:32:37.635Z'::timestamptz, NULL)
