  VALUES ('NEO', 112, 'Event form can never save — its type/status/attendees don''t match the encounter API', 'Found while building [NEO-109](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-109/form-errors-shown-in-the-form-inline-summary-not-as-toasts). The planner''s event form (EventForm) posts `type: "f2f" | "video"`, `status: "scheduled"` and attendee objects to `POST /api/v1/encounter`. The API only accepts:

* type: `visit | call | email | congress | webinar | other`
* status: `planned | completed | cancelled | no_show`
* attendees: `string[]`

So every save returns 400 "Invalid encounter type". Before [NEO-109](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-109/form-errors-shown-in-the-form-inline-summary-not-as-toasts) this showed as an "Error al guardar" toast. With [NEO-109](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-109/form-errors-shown-in-the-form-inline-summary-not-as-toasts) the form marks the Type field, but none of its options is valid, so the user can''t fix it.', 'Align the form''s values with the API contract (or the other way round), then check create + edit from Planner, HCO, lead views.',
    '* An event can be created and edited from the planner and the HCO/lead views.', 'done', 0, '{}'::text[],
