  VALUES ('NEO', 162, '"Send by email" on patient: email not received + doctor chooses which documents and how to send', 'Łukasz (2026-09-28): the patient''s "SEND BY EMAIL" button shows success, but no email arrives in his inbox.

Also: the doctor should pick which documents go out and in what form — e.g. a link to fill forms online, or blank PDFs to print and sign. What the button does needs to be thought through as a whole.

## Findings so far (diagnosis, no code changed)

* The button (`SendQuestionnaireEmailCommand`, `apps/api/src/commands/questionnaireRequest.ts`) emails the **patient''s own address** (`identities.email` of the patient), never the logged-in doctor. The email holds one personal link to every open questionnaire, with no attachments and no document names.
* The success toast only appears after Resend accepts the email; if Resend rejects it, the command throws and rolls back.
* Cloud Run dev logs, last 3 days: `Sent questionnaire link email to q@q.pl` (2026-09-27 09:28) and `... to kontakt@kaszebiweswiece.pl` (09:30). There were no email sends on 2026-09-28. One earlier send was rejected (an [example.com](<http://example.com>) address).
* The feature is on dev only, not prod.
* Not verified: the delivery status in the Resend dashboard (bounced, spam, or delivered).

## Decided scope (Łukasz, 2026-09-28/29)

* The "Send by email" button opens a dialog listing documents with an email preview. Documents the patient hasn''t filled or signed are pre-selected.
* The form is chosen per document. Anything still to be filled goes as an **online link**. Completed or signed copies go as **…', NULL,
    '* The cause of the non-delivery is confirmed and fixed, or explained.
* The doctor picks documents and a delivery mode, and it is implemented as decided.', 'backlog', 2, '{}'::text[],
    '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'linear_import', 'NEO-162', 'linear',
    '2026-09-28T13:45:22.819Z'::timestamptz, '2026-09-28T13:45:22.819Z'::timestamptz, '2026-09-28T13:45:22.819Z'::timestamptz, NULL)
  ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
  RETURNING id
)
