  VALUES ('NEO', 172, 'Patient email when their OrthoApnea order status changes', 'Until [NEO-134](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-134/engine-core-event-catalog-notify-and-delivery-log), a change in the status of a patient''s OrthoApnea order created an in-app inbox row for the patient, which nobody ever saw because patients have no login. [NEO-134](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-134/engine-core-event-catalog-notify-and-delivery-log) removed that row. Łukasz decided on 2026-09-28 that the patient should get an email instead.', '* Add a patient recipient to `partner_order_status_changed`, on the email channel only, with no in-app row.
* The email is PHI-free: "The status of your order has been updated", the clinic''s name and contact, and no product or clinical detail. It is sent in the patient''s language.
* It is sent only with email consent ([NEO-146](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-146/patient-contact-consent-per-channel-in-the-qr-consent-email-phonesms)). Without consent it is logged as `skipped_no_consent`.
* If the status changes several times within 5 minutes, only one email goes out (engine grouping).',
    '* A status change sends one email to a consenting patient and none to a patient without consent (test).
* Nothing in the email identifies the treatment (PHI guard test).
* A real email arrives on dev.', 'backlog', 3, ARRAY['Notifications', 'Feature']::text[],
