     source, linear_identifier, created_by, created_at, updated_at, status_changed_at, completed_at)
  VALUES ('NEO', 184, 'MX informed consent shows "QA consent body." — test overwrote the real text in the shared DB', 'Patients in MX see "QA consent body." instead of the real informed-consent text when they sign on the phone (screenshot from Łukasz, 2026-09-28).

Root cause: `apps/api/src/commands/patientChecklist.spec.ts` inserts a new *current* version of the real templates `informedConsent/mx` and `historiaEndo/mx` in `platform.document_content_version` and never restores it. Whenever that spec ran against the Supabase DB (root `.env`) instead of a local Postgres, the real text was pushed down. Real text (v3, Łukasz, 2026-09-16) is still in the history — nothing lost.

`historiaEndo/mx` never had real content in the DB (only QA rows).', '* Data: restore `informedConsent/mx` by saving v3''s text as a new current version (history stays intact — signed PDFs remain traceable).
* Code: specs that need content for a real template use the existing current text when there is one and only seed (and later remove) when there is none. Covers patientChecklist.spec.ts and questionnaireRequest.spec.ts.',
    '* The consent screen on pwa-dev shows the real MX consent text.
* Running the API test suite against a DB that already has real content leaves that content untouched (test proves it).

Related: every patient needs at least one signed informed consent — checklist already tracks it ([NEO-36](https://linear.app/neosleep/issue/NEO-36/historia-endo-intake-checklist-stop-bang-screening-printable-pdf)).', 'done', 1, ARRAY['Bug']::text[],
    '[{"kind":"pr","url":"https://github.com/lukasz512/NeoSleep/pull/336","title":"NEO-184 Tests never replace real consent text in the shared DB"},{"kind":"artifact","url":"https://claude.ai/artifact/LL4fGEMmtYpHUCNV1LiH5x","title":"Artifact: NEO-184 MX Consent Text Restored"}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'linear_import', 'NEO-184', 'linear',
