    (team_key, number, title, problem, change, done_when, status, priority, labels, links, branch,
     source, linear_identifier, created_by, created_at, updated_at, status_changed_at, completed_at)
  VALUES ('NEO', 253, 'Historia clínica print: Sexo box never ticked from the patient''s gender', 'The printed Historia Clínica leaves Mujer / Hombre / Otro all empty, even though every patient has a required gender on their record. The print only reads the STOP-Bang "G" answer (is_male), so women and patients with no screening always print blank.', 'Tick the Sexo box from the patient''s own gender (identities.gender: female → Mujer, male → Hombre, other → Otro, prefer_not_to_say → none). Fall back to the STOP-Bang is_male answer only when gender is missing.',
    '* Unit test: female/male/other patient prints the matching box ticked; prefer_not_to_say and missing gender stay blank.
* The Historia Clínica PDF for a female patient shows Mujer ticked.

Added in the same thread (Łukasz): the Clase esqueletal boxes (I/II/III) must be right-aligned on the same grid as the Sí/No boxes above. Fix: fixed-width option slots in .hc-q, so III sits under No and II under Sí.', 'done', 2, '{}'::text[],
    '[{"kind":"pr","url":"https://github.com/lukasz512/NeoSleep/pull/470","title":"NEO-253 Historia clínica: Sexo from patient gender, aligned class boxes"},{"kind":"artifact","url":"https://claude.ai/artifact/SiMNyDmpHDScZGxYjQtxUS","title":"Artifact: NEO-253 Historia Sexo + Class Boxes"}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'linear_import', 'NEO-253', 'linear',
    '2026-10-05T23:55:33.244Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-06T00:11:29.712Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-06T00:11:29.712Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-06T00:11:29.712Z'::timestamptz)
  ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
  RETURNING id
)
